<title>FINLAND: NorScan June pulp stocks down 60,000 tonnes-agency.</title>
<headline>NorScan June pulp stocks down 60,000 tonnes-agency.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>North American and Scandinavian (NorScan) pulp stocks fell by 60,000 tonnes to just under 1.6 million tonnes in June, the Finnish STT news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>STT, quoting the Finnish Forest Industries Federation, said the stocks at the beginning of the year were over two million tonnes but producer stoppages combined with good demand had caused the fall.</p>
<p>Pulp stocks are measured regularly in the United States, Canada, Sweden, Norway and Finland.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
